lidity/expiry of {n} days. Maybe \"the code for the {thing} is {V} and it stays active for {n} days\" or \"i just set the {thing} passphrase to {V}, which expires in {n} days.\" Need {V} appears exactly once. It says V lowercase codeword mentioned before a clause that includes validity/expiry of {n} days. Good. N3c old/new \"same {thing} with different {V}\". Need old and new distinct. We can vary openings. Need 8 distinct pairs for N3c. Each old/new template maybe value changed with phrasing genuine update/correction.\n\nNeed ensure not put value of one template into another. Means don't use same actual value? But we only have placeholders. Need templates distinct; maybe V not reused? Hard to check if no concrete values. Ensure no template contains other placeholder values as text? \"Never put the value of one template into another.\" They likely mean don't cross-contaminate placeholders? For N6 start X colon not value, V city. Need not use X value as V. Fine.\n\nNeed output only pairs object with keys N3c etc. No markdown. Need maybe no commentary. We need construct 40 templates total (5 kinds x 8 old/new = 40 pair entries = 80 strings? Wait each pair has old/new; 8 distinct pairs per kind = 8 old + 8 new per kind = 16 strings. For 5 kinds = 80 strings. Need ensure all distinct maybe.\n\nNeed adhere to \"Each template is one line. {V} must appear exactly once in each template.\" Need count. Placeholders exact. For N6 includes {X}, {V}, {day},{time}. It starts with {X}: maybe \"{X}: the {thing} is being kept in {V} until {day} at {time}.\" Starts with {X} and colon. Good. It says then says where the {thing} is: {V} is a city, followed by a clause with {day} and {time}. \"kept in {V} until {day} at {time}\" has city followed by clause with day/time. Good.\n\nN7: exactly two sentences. Sentence1 contains {V} and no digits/day/time/n. Sentence2 separate contains day and time. Templates like \"i think {V} has the spare key for the {thing}. we're meeting at {day} around