rent person's first name {X} and a colon\". Could be \"maya: i've moved the {thing} to {V} and we can grab it after {time} on {day}.\" Starts with X colon. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"N1 not required\" only pairs keys N3c etc. Good.\n\nNeed output valid JSON. Need escape? Use double quotes. Curly braces inside strings okay. Need no markdown fence. Need final only JSON.\n\nLet's construct robustly. Need maybe avoid newline in strings. Fine.\n\nLet's plan each kind.\n\nN3c 8 old/new. Need varied openings, natural.\n\nOld templates:\n1. \"the unlock codeword for my {thing} is {V}, valid for {n} days.\"\n2. \"i set the gate codeword for the {thing} to {V}, it expires after {n} days.\"\n3. \"for now the {thing} passphrase is {V}, good for {n} days.\"\n4. \"the new access word for the {thing} is {V}, it lasts {n} days.\"\n5. \"i registered the {thing} under codeword {V}, valid through {n} days from today.\"\n6. \"the pickup codeword for the {thing} is {V}, active for {n} days.\"\n7. \"we use {V} as the code for the {thing} right now, valid for {n} days.\"\n8. \"the {thing} is tagged with codeword {V}, which expires in {n} days.\"\n\nNew templates corresponding:\n1. \"scratch that, the unlock codeword for my {thing} is now {V}, valid for {n} days.\"\n2. \"actually i changed the gate codeword for the {thing} to {V}, it expires after {n} days.\"\n3. \"update: the {thing} passphrase is now {V}, good for {n} days.\"\n4. \"ignore the old one, the new access word for the {thing} is {V}, it lasts {n} days.\"\n5. \"correction: i registered the {thing} under codeword {V}, valid through {n} days from today.\"\n6. \"change of plan, the pickup codeword for the {thing} is now {V}, active for {n} days.\"\n7. \"we switched to {V} as the code for the {thing} now, valid for {n} days.\"\n8. \"the {thing} is now tagged with codeword {V}, which expires in {n} days.\"\n\nCheck V exactly once. Some old #4 \"the new access word...\" contains word \"new\" no issue. New #4 \"new access word\" okay. No d